[BEGIN]
  ObjTp=Hd
  Cmn1=TCP Client (Dynamic IP) v1.0\\\\Simpl# TCP client that matches the||1
  Cmn2=built-in SIMPL Windows TCP/IP Client\\symbol (Connect, Connect_FB,||1
  Cmn3=TX$, RX$, status) except the remote host is\\a serial input, not||1
  Cmn4=an IP-table / Address parameter. No IP-ID required.\\\\Hold Connect||1
  Cmn5=high to open the socket. Release Connect to close it.\\Address$||1
  Cmn6=is IPv4 or a hostname. Empty Address$ will not connect.\\A change||1
  Cmn7=to Address$ or Port_Override while Connect is high reconnects.\\
  Cmn8=Port_Override greater than 0 replaces the Port parameter; 0 uses||1
  Cmn9=Port.\\\\If the remote end drops while Connect is still high, the||1
  Cmn10=client waits\\100 ms then retries (same idea as the stock client||1
  Cmn11=on CUZ 3.029+).\\\\TX$ is sent as-is (no extra CR/LF) and only while||1
  Cmn12=connected. RX$ is a\\byte pipe, chunked at 250 characters.\\\\status||1
  Cmn13=(stock TCP/IP Client values):\\  0d  Not connected\\  1d  Waiting||1
  Cmn14=for connection\\  2d  Connected\\  3d  Connection failed\\  4d||2
  Cmn15=Connection broken remotely\\  5d  Connection broken locally\\  6d||1
  Cmn16=||1Performing DNS lookup\\  7d  DNS lookup failed\\  8d  DNS lookup||1
  Cmn17=resolved\\\\4-Series only. Keep Dynamic_TCP_Client.clz in this folder.
  Cmn18=\\\\VERSION HISTORY\\v1.0  2026-09-02  RGW\\- Initial public module
[END]
